right now president trump is continuing  to say there is widespread voter fraud  here in the state of nevada  but his campaign and state republicans  have yet to show more than several  isolated cases now one of those cases  involve a woman who died in 2017.  the i-team's david charns looking into  that and david you talked to this  woman's husband kirk cartel's wife rose  marie who  passed away three years ago she is one  of two cases of somebody who died on  clark county's voter rolls  they were sent a mail-in ballot and that  ballot was returned the question  now is though who voted for her  it was disbelief  just it made no sense to me kirk cartel  said he was surprised when he found out  his wife  who died in 2017 had sent in a mail-in  ballot  i was surprised because she passed away  three years ago i was surprised to even  get that  rosemary hartl died at 52 from breast  cancer  her name is still on clark county's  voter rolls and since  everyone in those roles got a ballot one  was sent to rose marie  but kirk says a ballot never got to his  house  that is pretty sickening to me to be  honest with you according to ballot  tracks the mail-in ballot was sent  october  9 and returned the day before election  day clark county officials say  rose marie's signature is a match to  what's on their records  registrar for elections joe gloria says  any illegal activity will be flagged  now keith hartle wonders who took  advantage of his grief  adding he's surprised his wife received  a ballot at all  it certainly brings up a lot of  discomfort  you know there's a pretty exhaustive  process you go through when someone  passes  and in a second case a man who died in  2017 also had a ballot cast in his name  but  election officials tell me it appears  his daughter actually sent  in that ballot and she never cast her  own ballot clark county has forwarded  these two cases up to the secretary of  state's office they're the ones who  actually investigate  i'm david charns 8 news now
 

